# Accessibility (Priority 2)

Target: **WCAG 2.1 AA** — recruiters and developers on varied devices.

## Document & Language

```tsx
<html lang={locale} dir={locale === 'fa' ? 'rtl' : 'ltr'}>
```

- Switch `lang` and `dir` together when locale changes
- Mixed-direction content: wrap LTR fragments (code, URLs) in `<span dir="ltr">`

## Keyboard & Focus

- All interactive elements reachable via Tab
- Never remove focus outline without `:focus-visible` replacement
- Skip link: first focusable element — i18n key `a11y.skipToContent`
- Mobile menu: focus trap when open; close on Escape; return focus to menu button

## Navigation

- `<nav aria-label={t('a11y.mainNav')}>`
- Current page: `aria-current="page"` on active link
- Locale switcher: accessible name — not icon-only without label

## Theme Toggle

- Button with `aria-label` describing action (switch to dark/light)
- Respect `prefers-color-scheme` default; persist choice in `localStorage`

## Forms (Contact)

```tsx
<label htmlFor="email">{t('contact.email')}</label>
<input
  id="email"
  type="email"
  autoComplete="email"
  aria-invalid={!!errors.email}
  aria-describedby={errors.email ? 'email-error' : undefined}
/>
{errors.email && (
  <p id="email-error" role="alert">{errors.email}</p>
)}
```

- Placeholder supplements label — never replaces it
- Submit: `aria-busy={isSubmitting}` during request
- Success/error: `aria-live="polite"` region

## Images & Media

- Profile photo: meaningful `alt` with name
- Project screenshots: describe UI purpose, not "screenshot"
- Decorative elements: `alt=""` and `aria-hidden="true"`

## Motion

- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`: disable scroll animations and non-essential transitions
- No auto-playing video; no flashing content

## Color & Contrast

- Text contrast ≥ 4.5:1 (normal), ≥ 3:1 (large text)
- Do not convey status by color alone — include text/icons
- Dark and light themes must both meet contrast requirements — see `ui-design.mdc`

## Headings

- Single `<h1>` per page
- Logical order; section titles as `<h2>`

## External Links

- Indicate opens external site when leaving portfolio — i18n `a11y.externalLink` (visually hidden or icon + sr-only)

## Touch Targets

- Minimum **44×44px** on mobile for buttons and nav items
